From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:26:15 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] os, internal/syscall/windows: free a held file's name in os.Remove

os.Remove deletes through DeleteFileW. On Windows 7, 8, 8.1 and some early
versions of Windows 10 a file deleted that way keeps its name while any
program still has it open.

Free the name at once in os.Remove as well. There os.Remove deletes a file
the way RemoveAll does (CL 713480, commit b31dc77, Go 1.26).

	                       before                 after
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 7, 8, 8.1,     os.Remove leaves the   the name is free at once
	some early Windows 10  file's name
	(file open elsewhere)
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 10 22H2, 11    the name is free at    the name is free at once
	                       once

Gate: version, then query (Windows 10 before 22H2) | Remembered: Y

